	(text "POWER\n- J7 XT30PW-M (15A) -> F1 15A NANO2 fuse -> Q5 AO4407A reverse-battery PFET (gate to GND via R39) -> VBAT.\n- Q4 AO4407A switches VBAT -> SERVO_PWR. SW3 pulls the gate low through R38; R28 holds Q4 off; C28 gives ~1ms soft start.\n- Board rating (calculated, not yet measured): see the engineering review. Servos must be rated for 8.4V (HV).\n- Electronics run from SERVO_PWR via D4 or USB VBUS via D5 -> REG_IN -> U9 AP63203 (3.8-32V in).\n- V_SENSE = SERVO_PWR x 39k/(100k+39k): 2.36V at 8.4V, inside the ESP32 11dB ADC range (150-2450mV).\n\nINTERFACES\n- Servo/ESC outputs: 1k series + 100k pull-down at each connector; outputs read LOW while the MCU is in reset.\n- J8 ESC: pin1 GND, pin3 ESC_SIG (IO13). Pin2 left open so an ESC BEC cannot back-feed the 2S rail.\n- No actuator on a strapping pin: IO12 = buzzer (pulled low by R26/R27), IO15 = IMU2_CS (10k pull-up), IO2 = white LED.\n- IMU1 (LSM6DSV32X) INT1 -> IO34, IMU2 (ASM330LHH) INT1 -> IO35 (input-only pins, no internal pulls).\n- I2C 3.3V: MS5611 0x77 (CSB=GND), LIS3MDL; 4.7k pull-ups R8/R9.\n- BZ1 TMB12A03 is an ACTIVE buzzer: drive IO12 high to beep.\n- USB D+/D- protected by U10 USBLC6-2SC6 (low-capacitance ESD array).\n\nLAYOUT\n- No copper pour, tracks or vias in the ESP32 antenna area.\n- No tracks or vias under the MEMS sensors (ST TN0018); MS5611 kept away from the buck converter.\n- High-current path on F.Cu/B.Cu power zones with solid pad connections."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 235.6487 304.695 0)
		(effects
